.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt VIOINPUT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vioinput
.Nd VirtIO absolute pointing device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "vioinput* at virtio?"
.Cd "wsmouse* at vioinput?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides support for VirtIO input devices that advertise absolute X
and Y axes.
Input events are exposed through the
.Xr wsmouse 4
interface as absolute pointer coordinates, buttons, and vertical wheel motion.
.Pp
The driver supports the VirtIO event and status queues.
The status queue is currently unused because keyboard LEDs and force feedback
are not part of the supported absolute-tablet profile.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr virtio 4 ,
.Xr wsmouse 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
device driver first appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
